{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_589ec792803291110b9db478e74e061c96941492738106d93b01e08ae353f2bb", "title": "Winfried Bischoff", "text": "Sir Winfried Franz Wilhelm \"Win\" Bischoff (born 10 May 1941) is an Anglo-German banker and former chairman of Lloyds Banking Group. He previously served as chairman and interim CEO of Citigroup in 2007. He was succeeded as CEO by Vikram Pandit on 11 December 2007. Bischoff stepped down as chairman on 23 February 2009 and was replaced by Richard Parsons. He has dual British and German citizenship.", "score": 40.6589}, {"id": "hp_doc_3d222f4033d4d71d53bd6d21e4cb526add406800cec3f77bce7bef9cfd52f048", "title": "Hussain Najadi", "text": "Hussain Najadi (c. 1938 – 29 July 2013) was an international banker born in Bahrain to parents of Persian origin. He was the Chairman & CEO of AIAK Group based in Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia.", "score": 18.1833}, {"id": "hp_doc_43c798be3afdc40aab138a0ae9eabc8c233f2df56acab24718d22493d294391a", "title": "Vikram Pandit", "text": "Vikram Shankar Pandit (born 14 January 1957) is an Indian-born American banker. He is the former chief executive of Citigroup, a position he held from December 2007 until he resigned on 16 October 2012.", "score": 15.316}], "remaining_searches": 2}
